From dbef5282deb1866059fe4f0fda3453c49d6e335b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Aug 2024 18:41:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/53] swdtb: introduce andes software DTB merger (#91)

1. configs: enable console record in ae350
2. swdtb: show swdtb merger entry message in console record

configs: enable console record in ae350:
To display messages before serial initialization, enable console record,
which allocates memory as a ring buffer. The printf function will place
strings into the output ring buffer of the console record. After serial
initialization is complete, messages from printf will no longer be placed
in the ring buffer but will be directly displayed on the console.

swdtb: show swdtb merger entry message in console record:
When building with the SWDTB=1 option, both console recording and
the SWDTB merger are enabled.

The SWDTB merger entry is placed in the board_fdt_blob_setup function,
which is the hook for the vendor board to obtain the FDT blob.

To display the SWDTB merger message in the console record's ring buffer,
the display function should be placed in spl_board_init_f,
which is the U-Boot SPL initialization function for the vendor board.

